From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 01:52:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 429/488] [DS4.1] Captured forwards write their outputs into
 the graph buffers

The model graph manager copied every replay's hidden states and three
auxiliary hidden states into its persistent buffers: four copies a
decode step. The DS4.1 target now declares buffers for a captured
forward's outputs (rows: the largest CUDA graph) and, while a graph is
being captured, its last norm and the auxiliary collapses write into
them. The manager uses a model's declared buffers as its persistent
outputs and skips the copy when a captured forward wrote there; other
models are unchanged.
